    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "\r\nHi! I wanted to share my experience.  \r\n\r\nI used to use Harpoon, but I switched to **Mini.Visits**. I really like it, but I felt it was missing something a UI list similar to **oil.nvim** or **mini.files**. Since `:Pick visits` already exists (which is great!), I decided to create a Harpoon-like integration with **Mini.Visits** to get that list functionality.  \r\n\r\nI set it up, and surprisingly, it worked! Here’s a demo video:  \r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4bef116e-6d01-4ce1-94af-f3469cd3363c\r\n\r\n\r\nAnd here’s my code:  \r\n[__visits.lua](https://github.com/krovuxdev/NeoClean/blob/dev/plugin/__visits.lua)  \r\n\r\n@echasnovski, what do you think? If you like the idea, I’d be happy to make a PR!  ",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Hi! I wanted to share my experience.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I used to use Harpoon, but I switched to <strong>Mini.Visits</strong>. I really like it, but I felt it was missing something a UI list similar to <strong>oil.nvim</strong> or <strong>mini.files</strong>. Since <code class=\"notranslate\">:Pick visits</code> already exists (which is great!), I decided to create a Harpoon-like integration with <strong>Mini.Visits</strong> to get that list functionality.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I set it up, and surprisingly, it worked! Here’s a demo video:</p>\n<details open=\"\" class=\"details-reset border rounded-2\">\n  <summary class=\"tmp-px-3 py-2\">\n    <svg aria-hidden=\"true\" data-component=\"Octicon\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" data-view-component=\"true\" class=\"octicon octicon-device-camera-video\">\n    <path d=\"M16 3.75v8.5a.75.75 0 0 1-1.136.643L11 10.575v.675A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 9.25 13h-7.5A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 0 11.25v-6.5C0 3.784.784 3 1.75 3h7.5c.966 0 1.75.784 1.75 1.75v.675l3.864-2.318A.75.75 0 0 1 16 3.75Zm-6.5 1a.25.25 0 0 0-.25-.25h-7.5a.25.25 0 0 0-.25.25v6.5c0 .138.112.25.25.25h7.5a.25.25 0 0 0 .25-.25v-6.5ZM11 8.825l3.5 2.1v-5.85l-3.5 2.1Z\"></path>\n</svg>\n    <span class=\"m-1\">harpoon-like.mp4</span>\n    <span class=\"dropdown-caret\"></span>\n  </summary>\n\n  <video src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/62192487/439839026-4bef116e-6d01-4ce1-94af-f3469cd3363c.mp4?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..yAjjCxu85B0WhR-xVTr58EiRWngwGZJIJC8CIjl1Cb8\" data-canonical-src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/62192487/439839026-4bef116e-6d01-4ce1-94af-f3469cd3363c.mp4?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..yAjjCxu85B0WhR-xVTr58EiRWngwGZJIJC8CIjl1Cb8\" controls=\"controls\" muted=\"muted\" class=\"d-block rounded-bottom-2 border-top width-fit\" style=\"max-height:640px; min-height: 200px\">\n\n  </video>\n</details>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">And here’s my code:<br>\n<a href=\"https://github.com/krovuxdev/NeoClean/blob/dev/plugin/__visits.lua\">__visits.lua</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/echasnovski/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski\">@echasnovski</a>, what do you think? If you like the idea, I’d be happy to make a PR!</p>",
    "bodyText": "Hi! I wanted to share my experience.\nI used to use Harpoon, but I switched to Mini.Visits. I really like it, but I felt it was missing something a UI list similar to oil.nvim or mini.files. Since :Pick visits already exists (which is great!), I decided to create a Harpoon-like integration with Mini.Visits to get that list functionality.\nI set it up, and surprisingly, it worked! Here’s a demo video:\n\n  \n    \n    \n\n    harpoon-like.mp4\n    \n  \n\n  \n\n  \n\n\nAnd here’s my code:\n__visits.lua\n@echasnovski, what do you think? If you like the idea, I’d be happy to make a PR!",
